    if [file], has a rule for, [word]
    and [fact pattern], names, [word]
    and [creator], creates fact, [fact pattern]
    and [creator], differs from, [file]

a workflow that fakes what the tools returned, adds line, workflow.plain, "command: a fake, returned, file, nowhere"
a workflow that fakes what the tools returned, must break, Each word has one creator

a spec that looks for itself, adds line, spec.plain, "ghost.txt, is, in the folder"
a spec that looks for itself, must break, Each word has one creator

"engine.go, loads, spec.plain", means in mangle, 'loads("engine.go", "spec.plain").'
"spec.plain, is, in the folder", means in mangle, in_the_folder("spec.plain").
a law is broken, means in mangle, a_law_is_broken().
"command: list the folder, uses, list, the folder", means in mangle, 'uses("command: list the folder", "list", "the folder").'
"[file], is, used", means in mangle, used(File).
"[any file], is, used", means in mangle, used(AnyFile).
"true, exits with, 0", means in mangle, 'exits_with("true", 0).'
'a change, adds line, notes.plain, "a, is, a note"', means in mangle, 'adds_line("a change", "notes.plain", "a, is, a note").'
"[file], ends with, [ending]", means in mangle, ":string:ends_with(File, Ending)"
"[command], starts with, [prefix]", means in mangle, ":string:starts_with(Command, Prefix)"
"[file], differs from, [other file]", means in mangle, File != OtherFile
'[command], is the join of, "command: count the lines of ", [file]', means in mangle, 'Command = fn:string:concat("command: count the lines of ", File)'
"declared: [rule], is, never fired", means in mangle, Decl never_fired(Rule).

[line], breaks, Every line reads back as written
    if [line], is, misread

a line that reads back differently, adds line, spec.plain, '"zzz", means, nothing'
a line that reads back differently, must break, Every line reads back as written

.plain, means, plain language
.go, means, go
go.mod, means, go module
go.sum, means, go checksums
.sh, means, sh

[file], written in, [language]
    if [file], is, in the folder
    and [ending], means, [language]
    and [file], ends with, [ending]
